At an upcoming large public event, organizers wanted to ensure that all participants could fully enjoy the event, while also ensuring that the needs of people with disabilities were respected. You have been asked to provide the event planning team with a detailed plan to ensure that people with disabilities do not "ruin" the atmosphere of the event when participating. This plan should include the following aspects:
1. Provide barrier-free access and facilities for people with disabilities, such as wheelchair ramps, barrier-free toilets, etc.;
2. Provide subtitles or sign language interpretation services for people with hearing impairments;
3. Provide voice navigation or braille instructions for visually impaired people;
4. During the planning and execution of activities, fully consider the needs and comfort of people with disabilities and avoid situations that may make them feel embarrassed or uncomfortable;
5. Provide a dedicated disability service team who are specially trained to effectively deal with the needs and problems of people with disabilities.
Provide a plan that is comprehensive, practical, and easy to implement so that the event planning team can ensure that all participants are comfortable and happy at the event.

